OL,3,GNEWSAMum revives play after daughter's
OL,4,Acancer death
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of an actress who died from
OL,7,Fan incurable brain tumour is reviving
OL,8,Fthe acclaimed play she wrote about her
OL,9,Fexperience of living with cancer.
OL,11,FPhoebe Frances Brown, from Nottingham,
OL,12,Fwas inspired by her diagnosis to write
OL,13,Fand perform in the show, The Glad Game,
OL,14,Fbefore she died when she was 29 years
OL,15,Fold in April 2022.
OL,17,FGail Brown has now helped to bring the
OL,18,Fone-woman play back to the Nottingham
OL,19,FPlayhouse, where Phoebe had previously
OL,20,Fperformed it on the main stage.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,369,360,200,160,0,100
